  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multiprofile+avgpool+pca_n2000 (config_002) achieves the best score so far (acc=0.591, F1=0.573), while image-only with resnet50 (config_010) is very weak (acc=0.208). This creates a critical uncertainty: does adding the image modality via fusion actually improve over the strong RNA-only baseline, or does the weak image signal introduce noise? Question tested: config_018 directly extends the best-known RNA configuration (multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) by adding resnet50 image features with simple concat fusion, testing whether multimodal fusion yields a net gain. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It resolves the single most impactful architectural question—whether the multimodal setting is worth pursuing at all—before investing budget in 36+ multimodal variants. (2) A positive result (>0.591) identifies a promising direction to exploit; a negative result efficiently rules out an entire family of configurations. (3) It uses the strongest known unimodal baseline as the control, making the comparison clean and interpretable. (4) Under a limited budget, this one experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-level design choice (unimodal vs. multimodal) before committing to lower-level choices (fusion type, image encoder, RNA encoder)."
}

